PRETABLE -- m88kexcdeliver repair 13 (probe v19 -> v20), written 2026-10-16 BEFORE table 16 runs (this file's mtime is the order proof).
Trigger: the 2026-10-16 four-seat adjudication (adj_20261016/m88kexcdeliver/).  Fable 5.1 ruled DO NOT CLOSE and predicted
`implemented = !cpu->delay_slot' at MISALIGN/UNIMPL/PRIV/OVF would sweep the 59-row instrument; MEASURED at HEAD 7b23b785 in the
WSL scratch clone /tmp/gxm88kds (delayslot_20261016/): all four 59/59, each probe log byte-identical to BASE (md5 898eb0a7).
Their polarity twins (`cpu->delay_slot ? true : false') were caught: OVF 50/59, MISALIGN 51/59, PRIV 53/59, UNIMPL 54/59.
Grade: L2 (a floor breach in the shipped composite detector), repaired in-round; the row is still "in work", so this is not a late dissent.

1. SIBLING PARITY.  The seven delivered switch-1 arms (MISALIGN 4, UNIMPL 5, PRIV 6, BOUNDS 7, DIV0 8, OVF 9, ERROR 10) all share
   the delivery body.  Only DIV0 had a row faulting IN A DELAY SLOT (`dslot').  Asymmetry -> rows owed at the other arms that a guest
   INSTRUCTION can raise from a delay slot: MISALIGN (ld with an odd address), UNIMPL (prom_call in user mode), PRIV (ldcr in user
   mode), OVF (add 0x7fffffff + 1).  BOUNDS and ERROR are raised by no instruction (only a trap instruction naming 7 or 10, or tbnd,
   which is not implemented -- row m88ktbnd); their delay-slot cell needs a TRAP INSTRUCTION IN A DELAY SLOT.  mc88100.txt:9433-9440
   (6.7.2 note 6) speaks of instructions in the delay slot OF a trap-taken instruction, never of a trap instruction IN a slot, so its
   legality is unsettled from the manual -> DISCLOSED, per the flagship ruling; both mutants are MEASURED in table 16 so the
   disclosure states a measured escape, not a prediction.  The trap route x {delay slot} at the five other arms (tb1 naming 4/5/6/8/9
   in a slot) is the same unsettled case -> disclosed with them.

2. CLAIM -> ROW.  The v20 contract sentence: "{class} x {delay slot}: DIV0 dslot, MISALIGNED dslotmisalign, UNIMPLEMENTED
   dslotunimpl, PRIVILEGE dslotpriv, OVERFLOW dslotovf" -> one row each.  "BOUNDS and ERROR x {delay slot}, and every trap
   instruction in a slot, are disclosed" -> no row, with the measured escape named (M_DSNOT_BOUNDS, M_DSNOT_ERROR).

3. GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD.  Guard: `implemented', assigned per arm, reads nothing in the shipped form.  The delivery body after the
   switch reads: vector, is_trap, cr[PSR] (SFRZ tested; the rest copied/ORed), cpu->delay_slot, cpu->pc, cd.m88k.delay_target,
   cr[VBR].  PARTITIONS THE BODY INDUCES: delay_slot {0, nonzero} (`if (cpu->delay_slot)'), and inside nonzero, vector {DATA_ACCESS,
   INSTRUCTION_ACCESS, other} -- all seven arms take `other' (the else-arm: SNIP = pc+4, SFIP = delay_target); is_trap {0, 1};
   PSR & SFRZ {0, 1}; VBR, pc and delay_target are NOT tested (no partition; vbrtb anchors VBR).  So the single-axis floor added
   here is {7 arms} x {delay_slot set}: DIV0 rowed, four owed (section 1), two disclosed.  EXHAUSTED after v20 at the five
   instruction-reachable arms; multi-axis joints (delay slot x SFRZ, delay slot x is_trap, delay slot x a PSR bit) stay clause (e).

4. CHANNEL, per new row (all: a br.n +16 immediately before the faulting word, so delay_target = fault_pc + 12 != fault_pc + 4).
   dslotmisalign  [br.n +16, ld r2,r3,0] r3 = DATA+1, fault 0x10008, entry 0x20
                  kills M_DSNOT_MISALIGN: the fallback HALT (`unimplemented vector=0x004' + `machines stopped') replaces DELIVER.
   dslotunimpl    [stcr r3,cr1 (user), br.n +16, prom_call] fault 0x1000c, entry 0x28, EPSR = PSR_USER
                  kills M_DSNOT_UNIMPL: HALT replaces DELIVER.
   dslotpriv      [stcr r3,cr1 (user), br.n +16, ldcr r2,cr1] fault 0x1000c, entry 0x30, EPSR = PSR_USER
                  kills M_DSNOT_PRIV: HALT replaces DELIVER.
   dslotovf       [br.n +16, add r2,r3,r4] r3 = 0x7fffffff r4 = 1, fault 0x10008, entry 0x48
                  kills M_DSNOT_OVF: HALT replaces DELIVER.
   Each row also pins the else-arm shadows for its arm (SNIP = fault_pc+4, SFIP = fault_pc+12) -- AS IMPLEMENTED, exactly as
   dslot does; m88kdslotshadow (the manual says the else-arm returns WRONG) re-pins all five rows in one place when it lands,
   because the five share one scoring branch.  The existing dslot row's want-dict is unchanged by the generalisation
   (CODE + 4 + 16 == 0x10008 + 12).

